From 4166e9690471870770e1d4568d1512c5ff2d8132 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aleksei Bukhalov <buhaloff.aleks@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 02:36:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] feat: persistent disk prompt-cache tier, increment 3
 (disk lookup on RAM miss)

LRUPromptCache gains an on_miss(model, tokens, ram_cache, ram_rest) hook,
called from fetch_nearest_cache only when the RAM answer left tokens
unconsumed (ram_rest non-empty) -- a RAM exact hit never triggers it.
Returning (cache, rest) overrides the RAM answer; None keeps it. The
original method body moves to _fetch_nearest_cache_ram unchanged.

DiskPromptStore.consult_and_promote implements the hook: exact / longer
(trim) / shorter disk matches, in that preference order, each only used
when at least as good as what RAM already had (a shorter disk match must
beat RAM's own reuse length). A hit is deep-copied into the RAM tier via
insert_cache before being handed to the caller, promoting it exactly the
way the original RAM-only trie's own longer/shorter branches already
avoid handing out the trie's live object.

server.py wires prompt_cache.on_miss to close over the disk_store and the
now-constructed prompt_cache (set after construction, since the closure
needs a reference to prompt_cache itself).

5 new tests (exact/longer/shorter disk promotion, RAM-hit-skips-on_miss);
all 9 tests in this file and all 23 upstream cache tests still pass.

Increment 3 of 3 (NOW.md Phase M1) -- the disk tier MVP is feature-complete.
Gate G1-MLX (cache disabled / RAM-only / RAM+disk, real restarts) is next.
